# Direct dependencies — the file to edit when adding or upgrading a package.
#
# requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file and pins every package,
# including transitive ones, to an exact version. CI and Render both install
# requirements.txt, so they get identical environments. Regenerate it after
# editing this file:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --python-version 3.11 --python-platform linux -o requirements.txt
#
# Why a lock: every spec here is `>=`, so installs used to resolve to whatever
# was newest on the day — and to *different* versions depending on the Python
# interpreter. CI and Render run Python 3.11; a Python 3.9 venv silently
# resolved older, 3.9-compatible releases of Alembic, FastAPI and Starlette.
# That is how a test passed locally on Starlette 0.49 while CI failed on 1.6,
# where included routers are no longer flattened into app.routes (#229).
#
# The lock targets Python 3.11. It will not install on 3.9 (alembic 1.20
# requires >=3.10), so a local venv needs Python 3.10+ — ideally 3.11 — to
# match CI and production.

